# The run archive is COMMITTED evidence and must never be touched: every file
# under runs/<id>/output/ is covered by that run's `run_manifest.json` hashes,
# so reformatting even one of them would make `verify-manifest` fail.
experiments/sime2026/runs/
experiments/sime2026/*.jsonl
experiments/sime2026/*.log
experiments/sime2026/*.csv
experiments/sime2026/*.csv.gz

# Committed experiment evidence, written by the experiment scripts. Prettier is
# kept off them so that a regeneration produces a content-only diff instead of a
# whole-file reformat: they are checked by re-running the script and comparing
# the numbers, not by Prettier.
#
# They are content-stable, NOT byte-stable, and no claim of byte-identity is
# made for them:
#   * E1-fairness-benchmark-results.md stamps the generation date
#     (scripts/fairness-benchmark.ts) and E5-label-agreement.md / .json stamp a
#     full timestamp (experiments/sime2026/label-agreement.ts), so those fields
#     change on every run;
#   * full-dataset-scan.md records machine-specific wall times and throughput;
#   * E1-fairness-benchmark-results.md, E3-payload-e4-224px.md and
#     full-dataset-scan.md were Prettier-formatted once before being listed
#     here, so their Markdown table padding differs from a fresh generator run
#     even where every number is identical.
# Re-deriving them is a check on the numbers, never a byte comparison.
experiments/sime2026/E1-fairness-benchmark-results.md
experiments/sime2026/E3-payload-*.md
experiments/sime2026/E5-label-agreement.md
experiments/sime2026/E5-label-agreement.json
experiments/sime2026/full-dataset-scan.md
experiments/sime2026/probe-results.md
experiments/sime2026/probe-results.json
experiments/sime2026/nih-selection.json
